+
+Let m and n be arbitrary finite index types, A and H square complex blocks and C an arbitrary m by n complex block. Assume S=[A,C;C star,H] is positive semidefinite, r is positive, and Z is Hermitian. Put P0=diag(I,rI), Y=P0 cubed and K=[A,r sqrt(r) C;r sqrt(r) C star,r cubed H]. The positive CFC cube root P=Y^(1/3) is exactly P0, and its actual matrix inverse is diag(I,r inverse I). Define F(t)=P inverse CFC.rpow(Y+tK,2/3) P inverse and B_j=F^(j)(0)/j factorial. These coefficients are genuine derivatives of the actual CFC function.
+
+The conclusion is 0 <= kappa(r) pairEnergy(A,C,H)/6 <= tr(B_3)+2 tr(Z B_2)+tr(B_1 Z Z)-(5/48) tr(B_1 cubed), where tr is real trace. The coefficient kappa and pairEnergy are the explicit quantities in HsfBalancedSpectralCertificate. No derivative, Taylor recurrence or desired inequality is a hypothesis. The direction S may be singular; repeated levels r=1, unequal block multiplicities and empty finite blocks are included.
+
+The proof uses Mathlib's positive diagonal and CFC power composition identities to establish positivity and the actual root and inverse. RpowPencilTaylor supplies the smooth root and its first three factorial-normalized ordered recurrences. Expanding the normalized two-thirds jet at orders one, two and three gives the three matrices in supplier_of_cubic_recurrence, which is then applied without commuting any matrix factors.
+
+**Theorem 1.2 (Transport by a common scale and fixed unitary coordinates).**
+
+Lean statement: `D5/S3/Quantum/Matrix/HsfBalancedCfcBridge.transported_twoLevel_supplier`
+
+*Proof.* Machine-checked in Lean as `D5/S3/Quantum/Matrix/HsfBalancedCfcBridge.transported_twoLevel_supplier` (`✓ std3`). ∎
+
+*Source.* Repository-derived.
+
+*Commentary.*
+
+Choose any equivalence q from the two block index types onto an arbitrary finite index type, any unitary U there, and any positive real c. The star-algebra equivalence spectralFrame reindexes by q and then conjugates by U. With e=spectralFrame(q,U), replace Y and K simultaneously by c e(Y) and c e(K). The same inequality holds for every Hermitian Z in the new coordinates, using real traces of the actual derivatives in those coordinates.
+
+The consumed transport proof establishes the actual CFC homogeneity and covariance identities for powers 1/3 and 2/3, identifies the actual inverse of the transported root, and cancels c^(2/3) against two factors c^(-1/3). The entire normalized function is conjugated by the fixed continuous real linear coordinate equivalence. This equivalence commutes with the factorial-normalized actual derivatives, and reindexing and unitary conjugation preserve real trace and Hermiticity. Arbitrary nonunitary congruence is outside this result.
+
+The theorem is parameterized by the chosen finite split, q, U, c and r. It does not construct such coordinates from a bare hypothesis that an input matrix has at most two eigenvalues. In the displayed frame, the center has positive levels c and c r cubed. No three-level or arbitrary-spectrum inequality follows from this result.
+
+This is a connection of classical finite dimensional CFC and inverse-function calculus to the finite weighted Gram certificate. The surrounding research target is He–Saunderson–Fawzi, arXiv:2502.05627v1 Conjecture 6.2 / DOI 10.1007/s10107-025-02314-0 Conjecture 1. No literature novelty or all-alpha, arbitrary-Y or independent-X,Y compatibility theorem is claimed.
+
+The two full-telescope typed registration attempts are compiled separately from the mathematical proof. Source-selection binding remains unfinished under https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/23103; declared_validated is not claimed.
+
